    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 1.19,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.12,
    "rationale": "The 18 h aliquot was read at three dilutions. At 10x the two replicates were 0.1185 and 0.1217, which scales to about 1.20. At 3x the reading was 0.4024, which scales to about 1.21. At 30x the reading was 0.039, which scales to about 1.17 and is noisier because the signal is low. The undiluted reading was 1.161. The dilution-corrected values are within about 3-4% of the undiluted reading and show no trend with dilution. If the reader were saturating, the corrected values would be well above the undiluted reading and would rise with dilution. The plateau at about 1.16 from 8 h onward therefore looks like real stationary phase and not a reader ceiling. A very small compression of about 3% at the top of the range is possible but is not meaningful."
